      "value": "@{5c96c04b5f368b2b23a7261d|full_name}: If what you are saying is true, then it would mean that having a custom trigger with any owner broadcast would be able to execute from anyone in the room calling with an owned object. This itself is a bad behavior and should still be fixed. No one would expect this as it makes it almost impossible to properly handle ownership transfer of objects.\n\nI originally found this bug by doing OnPlayerLeft OwnerUnbuffered all on a synced object and it only fired on master client causing things to break in unexpected ways. All the triggers were on the synced object. I also had an OwnerBufferOne trigger on the same object that only fired for the actual owner which just made this bug even weirder.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
