      "value": "@{5ae802a43ca0e56248e5cf8b|full_name}: Custom triggers with the Owner broadcast should behave the same way as a normal trigger I would imagine-- it would go through the list of referenced objects in the trigger and execute each one individually only if the player executing the trigger has ownership of the referenced object.\n\nBut I completely agree that it should be changed to check the ownership of the calling object rather than the referenced objects, but I imagine such a change would break a lot of worlds that already rely on the way it currently works.\n\nA good compromise might be giving us an option to choose between whether we want the calling object or referenced objects to be checked for ownership before executing the logic, and leave the default to the current behavior so existing worlds don't break from the change.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
