      "value": "@{5c96c04b5f368b2b23a7261d|full_name}: I think I misunderstood what you were saying before. In my world were OwnerBufferOne worked, I had the trigger on a synced object and it was only referencing objects that did not have ownership and were outside of the hierarchy. This is the behavior I expect. Similar to Master, Owner broadcasts should gate execution to only the owner of the object with the trigger, not the owner of the receivers on the trigger actions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
