      "value": "@{5ae802a43ca0e56248e5cf8b|full_name}: Can we be certain that the master broadcast actually gates execution from the object with the trigger and doesn't work similarly to owner? It might just seem that way since every object in the world would have the same master as the trigger object.\n\nThe reason I question it is because the owner broadcast shares the same buffer sync glitch as the master broadcast as mentioned in your other bug report post, so I wouldn't be surprised if their logic was shared or very much similar.\n\nFor your above example in your original post, I think I might have a solution. Try swapping the broadcasts around:\nChange the button from Local to Owner (with the appropriate buffer of your choice) and the custom trigger on your synced object from Owner to Local. That should change it to check for the ownership of the pickup rather than the cube you're having it turn on and off for 1 second.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
