      "value": "@{5c96c04b5f368b2b23a7261d|full_name}: Just tested and you are right for the case I created. Owner only affected receivers that the local player owns. Master could be the same thing but we have no way of testing this as all objects will return the same master client. This canny is no longer correct but I will make a different canny suggesting that ownership should be determined by the object the trigger is on instead of the receivers. At least I should be able to work with this now that I know what it is actually doing. This still doesn't fully explain how I was able to use it before where owner triggered as I expected for receivers that did not have any ownership in their hierarchy. Continuing my test, these objects are considered to be owned by Master.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
